DIALECT fork
------------

The files in this directory are modified forks, not byte-identical copies of the
official archive:

- CBaSE_params_v1.2.py
  SHA-256 d3721916eaffbef7ce138f703a219849780fbcc1171b6e8d6b3833d9fd51474c
- CBaSE_qvals_v1.2.py
  SHA-256 f626d9857db455eecc7b6093b9c23396d22aac92308a3475767871733bb154ff
- cbase_cohort_size.py
  SHA-256 381a91aa575c90868ec088b21267c9320a364e2b17ff7fcaeac50c1c527d1d69

Relative to the official v1.2 scripts, DIALECT's functional integration changes:

- preserve sample identifiers and repair the expected tab-delimited mutation input;
- accept explicit input, output, auxiliary-data, interpreter, and execution paths;
- reconcile the distributed auxiliary filename and DIALECT output naming;
- expose the PMF tail threshold instead of fixing one threshold for every cohort;
- preserve high-count PMF values through arbitrary-precision serialization before
  DIALECT's downstream deterministic conversion;
- derive and verify the cohort size from the authoritative selected sample axis; and
- include Python-compatibility, formatting, and lint maintenance needed by the
  packaged workflow.

The last functional provenance boundary for the explicit cohort-axis binding is
DIALECT commit d588383. Later release receipts must record the exact invoked
parameters, auxiliary inputs, runtime, source hashes, and output hashes; this notice
does not substitute for those run-specific receipts.
